+For a score of 95, compare two independent conditions `score >= 60` and `score >= 90` with an `if`/`else-if` chain in the same order. Predict how many messages each form prints. Then decide which order a chain needs if exactly one of “Pass” and “Distinction” is intended.
+
+```{dropdown} Trace and boundary check
+The independent `if` statements print both messages because both tests are true. The chain with `>= 60` first prints only “Pass”; it never tests its second condition. Put `>= 90` first when distinction takes priority. Check 59, 60, 89, 90, and 95: the intended categories are no pass, pass, pass, distinction, and distinction. A final `else` handles the no-pass case; a separate domain check handles invalid scores such as -1 or 101. These are different requirements.
+```
